{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"fc5e07c0-5323-410e-b4b1-6c7d202932ca","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Added the `codex-sandboxed` lane to [`run.sh`](file:///tmp/h-JtqllZ/run.sh) and documented the changes in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-JtqllZ/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Sandboxed Runner Function (`codex_sandboxed_run`)**:\n   - Matches the mechanism used in `kimi_run`:\n     - Creates a temporary scratch directory for `HOME` (`SH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/chome-XXXXXX)`).\n     - Exports `HOME=\"$SH\"` and invokes `sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\"`.\n     - Executes the identical Codex command line (`timeout $TO codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C \"$W\" --json -o \"$R/final.txt\" \"$P\" \u003c /dev/null \u003e \"$R/agent.log\" 2\u003e \"$R/agent.err\"`).\n     - Cleans up the scratch directory afterwards.\n2. **Lane Handling**:\n   - Added `codex-sandboxed) codex_sandboxed_run;;` to the `case $A in` switch statement.\n   - Updated the header comment documenting supported lanes.\n3. **Documentation**:\n   - Recorded the changes in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///tmp/h-JtqllZ/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":118.455061,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":150912,"output_tokens":3068,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":298180,"total_tokens":153980}}}
